course: dictionary
lesson: 12551
title: Detriment: when something causes harm
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: Detriment is a formal word for harm or damage. It means something bad happens to something else. «Staying up late was to the detriment of her health.» That means staying up late harmed her health. Look for the clue: is something being hurt or made worse?
explain: You will often see the phrase «to the detriment of». It goes before the thing that gets harmed. «Eating only sweets is to the detriment of your teeth» means sweets damage your teeth. Read it, then swap in «harm»: «Eating only sweets is harmful to your teeth». It still makes sense, so you have got it.
explain: The phrase «without detriment to» means the opposite. «The new road was built without detriment to the forest» means the forest was not harmed. Look for the word «without», which tells you there was no damage.
fact: Detriment is a noun. It names a harm or a loss.
fact: Detriment is formal, so you will mostly see it in writing, not in everyday chat.
fact: «To the detriment of» means harming something. For example, «to the detriment of your sleep».
fact: «Without detriment to» means without harming something, so the thing stays safe.
fact: Detriment is often used with words like health, sleep, learning, and teeth.
exercise: «Too much screen time is to the detriment of sleep.» What does detriment mean here? | Extra fun time | A good rest | A bright light | *Harm or damage
exercise: «The new road was built without detriment to the forest.» What does this tell you? | The forest was made very loud | The forest was harmed a great deal | *The forest was not harmed | The forest was painted green
exercise: «Eating only sweets can be a detriment to your teeth.» Find and copy the word that names the harm. | only | teeth | *detriment | sweets
test: «Lack of sleep was to the detriment of her learning.» Detriment is closest in meaning to: | Fun | *Harm | Practice | Help
test: Mum says, «Playing games all night will be to your detriment.» What does she mean? | It will be fun for you | *It will harm you | It will teach you a new game | It will reward you
exam: «Skipping breakfast can be to the detriment of your concentration.» What does detriment mean? | A quick rest | A gift | A cooked meal | *Harm or damage
